Below is the root cause and a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch to fix it.

1. Bug root cause  
In the CSS highlighter, comments are only recognized at the top level (`hljs.C_BLOCK_COMMENT_MODE` is in the root `contains`), but the property-value rule

```js
{
  begin: ':',
  end: '[;}]',
  contains: [ /* … */ ]
}
```

does not include `hljs.C_BLOCK_COMMENT_MODE` in its own `contains`. As a result any `/* … */` inside a declaration––for example  
```css
width: /* inline comment */ 50px;
```  
––is never tokenized as a comment.

2. Fix  
Add `hljs.C_BLOCK_COMMENT_MODE` as the first item in the `contains` array of the property-value mode.

